g in excel right so  crunching numbers  in excel working with spreadsheets  getting insights out of data  but then also your contribution in team  problem solving sessions so if you're  sitting together with your team  maybe your partner is flying in with  your project lead with other team  colleagues  you're debating a problem from your work  from the project how well  are you to contribute to that how much  of a value add  are you to solve the problems at hand  that the team is facing  all of this is part of your analytical  abilities and all of this will be  measured in this regard so let's now  talk about how a good consultant  distinguishes him or herself from a  great consultant  in regards to these analytical abilities  so a good consultant is doing well what  he or she is being told so you might sit  together with a project lead the project  lead provides you a data set  and the project need asks you to conduct  an analysis based on this data set  so a good consultant would do exactly  that would prepare a clean  nice analysis would crunch the numbers  get to a result  but the great consultant would go one  step further the great consultant in the  middle of the analysis might realize  that the actual question at hand cannot  really be answered by these  numbers that are included in the data  set this great consultant would realize  that probably he or she would need some  other data inputs to really get to a  great conclusion so instead of now just  doing just completing this analysis  because this  is what the project lee told him or  herself the great consultant would go  out  potentially talk to another client get  this data that would  actually be needed then integrate it in  the analysis  and then just prepare the good final  result that then really also answers the  question at hand  the second evaluation criterion i want  to talk about are your team abilities  so what exactly does this mean team  abilities well this is how well you  contribute  to the overall success of a team are you  just a lonely wolf just working for  yourself  or are you actually a team player also  supporting other people supporting the  team  your one question always is to what  extent you really contribute to a  positive and inclusive atmosphere in the  team room  sometimes things can be tough your team  might struggle with a difficult client  maybe you need to work late for several  days in a row  and all these things can really take a  toll on team morale  are you then the person who always  complains adds to all this negativity  draws everybody down or are you the  person who despite difficult  circumstances  is able to increase the team morale to  contribute to create  and add to an overall positive  atmosphere this is always a key question  that also i like to use when evaluating  teammates  on this criterion but then it's also  about other things how you communicate  how you work together with your  teammates  so if you get some tasks from your  project lead are you reliable  can you be trusted that you get that  done that you really will do your very  very best to complete the task as you've  been asked or maybe you see your  teammate is struggling with something  are you taking the time to sit together  with a teammate maybe it's a teammate  which is a bit more junior than you  maybe it's an intern  are you taking the time to help that  intern to develop that intern  all of these are qualities which are  looked at which are considered when  making this decision  so again let's talk about what  distinguishes a good consultant from a  great consultant when we talk about  these theme abilities  a good consultant in this regard is  reliable he or she would get all the  things done and then the project lead  us that consulted to do and if indeed  the project lead would ask that  consultant  to potentially also pick up some tasks  from another colleague even though these  tasks are not necessarily part  of your work stream that you're  responsible for then you would happily  do that as a good consultant the great  consultant would go one step  further so let's think back about the  situation where maybe things  are a bit tough team morale is down  things are a bit difficult at the moment  the great consultant would take  initiative would ask him or herself  what can i really do personally to  contribute to that and here one of the  things that this great consultant then  could do is to suggest to do a team  event  and this great consultant could then  even research potential things that  could be done  close to the office location could  organize a door  book it into the calendars make sure  that everybody is having a good time  these things are always great because of  course it's difficult to do this on top  of all your other duties  also for the project lead doing things  like that organizing things like that on  top of everything else can be quite a  burden so everybody will be super happy  if you're taking care of this and of  course if you do this proactively just  taking the initiative  organizing this this will always be  considered to be a great team player  just great contributing to the overall  team atmosphere  the third evaluation criterion are your  client abilities so how well  are you to work with and interact with  your clients and this can take all kinds  of forms  for sure your ability to lead client  meetings to lead interviews with clients  to communicate  things away to clients will play a role  here also often your abilities to create  written documents that are then  presented in front of clients that are  shown in front of clients  goes into that as well but here also  your overall ability to build a  trust-based relationship  but the extent to which the client  really wants to work with you because  the client sees you as a trusted advisor  with whom he or she would love to talk  to use you as a sparing's partner  get some feedback from you on ideas on  all kinds of topics that the client is  currently working on  and trust me as a project lead you  notice that  you notice if a client just randomly  walks into your team room  and wants to talk to some of your  consultants because the client really  enjoys talking to the person just would  love to get an opinion  on that person and here for sure a good  junior consultant would be able to build  a great working relationship with a  consultant  where you can in an effective way work  together exchange some ideas iterate on  some documents really work on an  end product together but the great  consultant would go one step  further so not only is this consulting  using the client to get some information  to get some data but the consultant  would really want to build a  relationship with a client the  relationship where both parties benefit  a relationship where potentially even  after the end of the project  both of you will stay in touch because  especially when you then get more and  more senior  these relationships are for sure  insanely important  because these relationships are the  starting position  of new projects of new client  discussions and then potentially  follow-on projects  might evolve on in the future and here  one tip that i got from a project lead i  worked with in one of my first projects  was that on  every single project you should try to  pick at least one person  at least one client with whom you really  enjoy working  and then try to build a friendship with  this client try to stay in contact  right to this client every six month or  so stay in contact  with this person just to build also your  professional network  because maybe this client at the time  when you work with this person  isn't even that senior isn't even that  important in the client organization but  in the same way that you progress  throughout your career  the same way often than clients are  progressing through their career as well  so a junior client who is junior today  maybe in three four five six seven years  once you are partner  is a pretty important pretty senior  client indeed and if you start building  your professional network like this  early on  chances are pretty high that besides all  the other benefits that you of course  also have by  gaining your valuable contact by  expanding your network chances are  higher  than this will really benefit you also  in the long term goal of potentially  acquiring new projects for your firm  i'd love to hear from you now what is  your experience with evaluation  processes so if you have any tips you'd  like to share just write a comment below  in the comment section  and as you know i do my very best to  answer every single comment that you  write  if you took any value out of this video  at all please hit the like button for  the youtube algorithm  and also subscribe to this channel to  stay up to date on all my content i also  started to become more active on both  twitch and tick tock so check that out  as well there's a link to that in the  video description i'd  also like to give a shout out to all the  members of firm learning thanks so much  for your support  and if you want to continue your  learning journey i suggest you check out  the video on the up or out principle  which is very closely related to  everything we just discussed today so  we'll link it somewhere above here check  it out to learn more about this  my name is heinrich i'm the creator of  from learning i release new videos  every single week here on my channel so  see you again next saturday  good weekend to all of you and bye bye

